            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0555" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.116 Autos/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-15T14:00:00-05:00">November 15, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. Your 209, November 6, 5 p.m.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d362-f1"/> In view of
                    reported new German restrictions on American automotive imports, the Department
                    requests that you follow the matter carefully and submit a full report as early
                    as practicable indicating whether discrimination is involved.</p>
                <p>If so, please take steps in the proper quarter to reserve our position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
